  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5552",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to be a multifaceted compound with multiple targets, all of which ultimately lead to MEL-JUSO through a series of biochemical pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N interacts with Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and this compound further targets MEL-JUSO. Similarly, Mollicellin N is also shown to interact with A704, which is a target of the same compound, and this pathway also leads to MEL-JUSO. Additionally, Mollicellin N is linked to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a different compound that also leads to MEL-JUSO. These findings collectively suggest that Mollicellin N may act through multiple distinct mechanisms, each involving different molecular targets, but all ultimately contributing to the interaction with MEL-JUSO. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular interactions and the potential for Mollicellin N to exert its effects through various routes, possibly modulating cellular processes that are critical for MEL-JUSO function.",
